; A later transaction with an already-seen UUID that carries more
; postings than the earlier one is not a duplicate: reading it reports
; the mismatch instead of comparing past the end of the shorter list.

2024/01/15 Store
    ; UUID: extra-1
    Expenses:Food       $50.00
    Assets:Cash

2024/01/15 Store
    ; UUID: extra-1
    Expenses:Food       $50.00
    Assets:Cash
    (Zzz:V1)             $1.00
    (Zzz:V2)             $2.00
    (Zzz:V3)             $3.00

test bal --columns=80 -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 16:
While comparing this previously seen transaction:
> 2024/01/15 Store
>     ; UUID: extra-1
>     Expenses:Food       $50.00
>     Assets:Cash
to this later transaction:
> 2024/01/15 Store
>     ; UUID: extra-1
>     Expenses:Food       $50.00
>     Assets:Cash
>     (Zzz:V1)             $1.00
>     (Zzz:V2)             $2.00
>     (Zzz:V3)             $3.00
Error: Transactions with the same UUID must have equivalent postings
end test
